    "statement": "\n    (n : ℕ) (f : (Fin n → ℝ) → ℝ)\n    (hf : ContDiff ℝ 2 f) (hs : HasCompactSupport f) :\n    let γ : Measure (Fin n → ℝ) := Measure.pi (fun _ : Fin n => gaussianReal 0 1)\n    let D : Fin n → (Fin n → ℝ) → ℝ := fun i x => fderiv ℝ f x (Pi.single i 1)\n    Integrable (fun x => (f x)^2) γ ∧\n    Integrable (fun x => (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2)) γ ∧\n    (∀ i, Integrable (fun x => (D i x)^2) γ) ∧\n    Integrable (fun x => ∑ i, (D i x)^2) γ ∧\n    (∫ x, (f x)^2 * Real.log ((f x)^2) ∂γ) -\n      (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) * Real.log (∫ x, (f x)^2 ∂γ) ≤\n    2 * ∫ x, ∑ i, (D i x)^2 ∂γ",
    "statement_sha256": "e3321973605f4ac1fd58ffc17a4eca9eb9d9f6b82e757076dd8e33093c5fc936",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "n is any natural number including0; f is an actual signed real function on Fin n -> Real with the default Pi topology/norm and Borel measurable structure.",
      "ContDiff Real2 means twice continuously Frechet differentiable; HasCompactSupport means the closure of the nonzero support is compact. They are the only analytic premises.",
      "The displayed gamma is the literal Measure.pi of actual independent centered variance-one scalar Gaussian laws. At n0 it is the probability law of the singleton empty-coordinate carrier.",
      "fderiv is the real Frechet derivative and Pi.single i1 is the literal coordinate direction. Energy is the displayed finite sum of squared directions; it is not norm(fderiv)^2 on the default Pi sup norm.",
      "All integrals are real Bochner integrals. Integrable conclusions assert genuine L1 domains for square, square-times-log, every coordinate square and their finite sum under the actual gamma.",
      "Real.log is totalized including zero. The displayed entropy is homogeneous without a unit-mass normalization assumption; signed f and zero function/mass are included. No positivity, L1, desired inequality or limit certificate is a public premise."
